'''Esports World Cup 2025''' serves as the final championship of the third season of the [[ESL Pro Tour]]. In preceding years it was held as ''Riyadh Masters'', it was announced as part of the [[esports:Esports_World_Cup/2025|Esports World Cup]] line-up on December 4, 2024.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ewc_en/status/1864308688145797212|title=It’s happening #Dota2 returns to #EWC2025 this summer!|author=Esports World Cup|date=2024-12-04}}</ref>

:''See [[esports:Esports_World_Cup/2025|here]] to read about the Esports World Cup 2025, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''

==Format==
*'''Phase 1 - Group Stage''' ''(July 8 - July 11)''
**Four groups of four teams in round-robin
**All series consist of two games
**{{Bgcolortext|up|Top team}} from each group advance to Phase 3
**{{Bgcolortext|stayup|2nd place team}} from each group advance to second round of Phase 2
**{{Bgcolortext|stay|Remaining teams}} from each group advance to first round of Phase 2
**{{collapsible rules|1|title=Click here for Group Stage tiebreaker rules|texts=
*If the tie is over a position of significance;
**Two teams - a {{Abbr/Bo3}} will be played
**Three teams or more - a {{Abbr/Bo1}} round-robin will be played
***If the tiebreaker does not resolve following the first round of the round robin
****Three teams - the tiebreaker will be replayed
****Four teams or more - the matrix listed below will be used to resolve the tie, adding the information from the tiebreaker matches to those gathered during the group stage
*For ties that are not over positions of significance (in order of importance):
*#Neustadtl score
*#Head-to-head record between the tied participants taking only game score into account
*#Record vs the first team below the tied teams, continuing to each subsequent team below the tied teams til the tie is resolved
*#1v1 tiebreakers
}}

*'''Phase 2 - Elimination Phase''' ''(July 12 - July 13'')
**Gauntlet bracket
**4th vs 3rd from groups, winner vs 2nd
**Four teams advance to Phase 3
**All matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}

*'''Phase 3 - Playoffs''' ''(July 16 - July 19)''
**Single-elimination bracket with third-placed match
**Grand Final is {{Abbr/Bo5}}, all other matches are {{Abbr/Bo3}}

