'''Riyadh Masters 2024''' is the third edition of the Riyadh Masters series, and serves as the final championship of the second season of the [[ESL Pro Tour]]. It was announced as part of the [[#Esports World Cup|Esports World Cup]] line-up on February 5, 2024.<ref name="EWC D2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ESWCgg/status/1754535355917750719|title=Dota 2 fans, get ready to be swept off your feet|date=2024-02-05|author=Esports World Cup}}</ref>

==Format==
*'''Participants'''
**Eight teams from [[ESL Pro Tour/Leaderboard/Season 2|EPT Leaderboard]] are seeded into group stage
**Twelve teams from regional qualifiers are seeded into play-in
***Three teams from China
***Two teams each from Western Europe, Southeast Asia, and South America
***One team each from Eastern Europe, MENA, and North America

*'''Play-In''' - ''July 4 - July 7, 2024''
**Two groups of six teams each
**Single round-robin
**All matches are {{Abbr/Bo2}}
**{{Bgcolortext|up|Top three teams}} from each group advance to the group stage
**{{Bgcolortext|stay|4th to 5th place team}} from each group will be matched
**{{Bgcolortext|down|Remaining teams}} are eliminated
***Matches are played from opposite groups
****{{Bgcolortext|up|Winners}} will advance to group stage
****{{Bgcolortext|down|Losers}} are eliminated
**<span class="mw-customtoggle-TiebreakerPI" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for Play-In tiebreaker rules''</span>
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-TiebreakerPI" style="width:750px; margin-left:45px">
*If the tie is over a position of significance;
**Two teams - a {{Abbr/Bo3}} will be played 
**Three teams or more - a {{Abbr/Bo1}} round-robin will be played
***If the tiebreaker does not resolve following the first round of the round robin
****Three teams - the tiebreaker will be replayed
****Four teams or more - the matrix listed below will be used to resolve the tie, adding the information from the tiebreaker matches to those gathered during the play-in proper
**If there is no schedule allowance, then 1v1 tiebreakers will be played
*For ties that are not over positions of significance (in order of importance):
*#[[wikipedia:Sonneborn–Berger_score|Neustadtl score]]
*#Head-to-head record between the tied participants taking only game score into account
*#Record vs the first team below the tied teams, continuing to each subsequent team below the tied teams til the tie is resolved
*#1v1 tiebreakers
</div>

*'''Group Stage''' - ''July 10 - July 14, 2024''
**Two groups of eight teams each
**Single round-robin
**All matches are {{Abbr/Bo2}}
**{{Bgcolortext|up|Top four teams}} from each group advance to the upper bracket of the playoffs
**{{Bgcolortext|stay|5th and 6th place team}} from each group advance to the lower bracket of the playoffs
**{{Bgcolortext|down|Remaining teams}} are eliminated
**<span class="mw-customtoggle-TiebreakerGS" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Click here for Group Stage tiebreaker rules''</span>
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-TiebreakerGS" style="width:750px; margin-left:45px">
*If the tie is over a position of significance;
**Two teams - a {{Abbr/Bo3}} will be played 
**Three teams or more - a {{Abbr/Bo1}} round-robin will be played
***If the tiebreaker does not resolve following the first round of the round robin
****Three teams - the tiebreaker will be replayed
****Four teams or more - the matrix listed below will be used to resolve the tie, adding the information from the tiebreaker matches to those gathered during the play-in proper
**If there is no schedule allowance, then 1v1 tiebreakers will be played
*For ties that are not over positions of significance (in order of importance):
*#[[wikipedia:Sonneborn–Berger_score|Neustadtl score]]
*#Head-to-head record between the tied participants taking only game score into account
*#Record vs the first team below the tied teams, continuing to each subsequent team below the tied teams til the tie is resolved
*#1v1 tiebreakers
</div>

*'''Playoffs''' - ''July 16 - July 21, 2024''
**Double-elimination bracket
**All matches except Grand Final are {{Abbr/Bo3}}
**Grand Final is {{Abbr/Bo5}}

