===Esports World Cup===
:''See also: [[esports:Esports World Cup/2024|Esports World Cup 2024]]''
Riyadh Masters 2024 was announced as part of the [[esports:Esports_World_Cup/2024|Esports World Cup]] line-up on February 5, 2024,<ref name="EWC D2"/> building off the [[Gamers8]] series that took place the [[Riyadh Masters/2023|year before]].  This brings together major tournaments across multiple esports titles in one umbrella event, held between June and August 2024.  Riyadh Masters 2024 serves as the ''Dota 2'' championship event, and the [[ESL Pro Tour]] serves as its qualifiers.

As part of the Esports World Cup, teams earn prize money for their performances across different esports titles within the Esports World Cup.  Select teams may also be chosen as part of the [[esports:Esports World Cup/2024#Esports World Cup Club Program|Esports World Cup Club Program]] for a stipend to support their operations, to fund their entry into new titles, and to receive money in driving viewership and engagement to the event.

